/T (Joe E.)
/Contents (Monatomic hydrogen would have had little cooling effect at lower temperatures \(<8000K\). This is partly due to it only having high-energy electronic transitions. We can contrast this with its triatomic form, where H_3^+ can have significant cooling effects at as low as 200K.)
